       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I'm not aware of any standard protocol that uses amlodipine 50 mg daily. The dose is five times the labeled maximum, and the harm could be severe and slow to reverse. I don't think an unverified statement is enough to justify entering it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and you can titrate later.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If the protocol is real, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through your hospital's high-dose override process. That path leaves a documented, verifiable record.\n- **Reference the protocol.** If you give me the protocol name or ID, I can include it in the order note. I still can't confirm it myself, so I'd want the order to go through that verification step.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
